  "scope": [
    "The entire production nonce() function is extracted byte-for-byte and compiled unchanged with private module aliases. No production module or nonce body is edited for positive controls.",
    "Unix/Bytes fault shims inject named finite exceptions/results while delegating actual random-file opens, reads and closes to the native Unix module.",
    "Successful nonce length is 32 and consumes 32 actual OS random bytes; owned descriptors settle once.",
    "Constructor OOM precedes native open; native open failure, post-open read-dispatch OOM, read failure, initial/partial EOF, finite EINTR plus short reads and consumed-close EIO preserve the specified primary errors.",
    "Three reuse controls close the random descriptor, immediately allocate a regular synthetic sentinel at that exact descriptor number, and verify its inode/type/content survive source cleanup retry paths.",
    "Pinned original e9be473 function opens an actual descriptor before constructor OOM: the negative measures the live leaked descriptor before fixture cleanup and rejects the regression.",
    "The private unchecked-close negative measures two native closes and a lost reused sentinel, then rejects the regression. All positive and negative fixture-owned descriptors are observed closed before fixture completion."
  ],
  "production_function_source_review": {
    "reviewer": "/root/scratch_integration",
    "observed": "Buffer, ownership flag and read/close callbacks precede open. The post-open read/close/result path is guarded, close clears ownership before the native call, and cleanup exceptions preserve the first error.",
    "scope": "Read-only review of the extracted function and named finite fault contract; no whole-module RPC or native transfer proof."
  },
